WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hi, my friend!
-Hello, friend.

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:04.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I am so --
We were talking backstage.

00:00:04.104 --> 00:00:06.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
The first two episodes
of "Barry" that I watched --

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:08.341 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's just fantastic.
-Oh, thank you.

00:00:08.341 --> 00:00:10.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You play a hitman.
-Uh-huh.

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:12.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Who wants to become an actor.
-Uh-huh.

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:13.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How --
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
How did you come up
with that idea?

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:18.118 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:19.085 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I don't know.

00:00:19.085 --> 00:00:20.120 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:23.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, it was this thing
where Alec Berg,

00:00:23.089 --> 00:00:24.524 align:start size:94% position:6%
who I co-created the show
with...

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:25.258 line:92%
-He's a fantastic writer.

00:00:25.258 --> 00:00:27.927
-He does "Silicon Valley"
and -- and a lot of things.

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:28.628 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We just thought --

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:30.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I said,
"What if I played a hitman?"

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:32.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he went,
"Oh, I hate the word --

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:34.434 align:start size:94% position:6%
just 'hitman,'
just what it conjures up,

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
like cool guy
and two guns and everything."

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.338 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like,
"No, but it will be me."

00:00:38.338 --> 00:00:39.672 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:42.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And he started laughing.
-Uh-huh.

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:43.410 line:92%
-And he went, "No, serious."

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.378 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"No, me as a hitman.

00:00:45.378 --> 00:00:48.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
And what if he was a former
Marine?" -- whatever.

00:00:48.448 --> 00:00:49.883 line:92%
And then, very quickly, somehow,

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:53.286
we just thought, "Oh,
he should take an acting class."

00:00:53.286 --> 00:00:54.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:55.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't know.
And then --

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:57.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we went in to HBO
and said,

00:00:57.157 --> 00:00:59.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Yeah, I'm a hitman
who takes an acting class."

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:03.797
And they -- they just went, "Um,
all right, yeah, sure, sure."

00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:04.330 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:06.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You directed the first three?
-That's right, yeah.

00:01:06.633 --> 00:01:07.434 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Was that something that

00:01:07.434 --> 00:01:09.135
you knew
as soon as you were doing a show

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:10.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you wanted to direct
some of them?

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:11.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah,
I really wanted to direct.

00:01:11.504 --> 00:01:14.307
That's kind of what
I wanted to do before, you know,

00:01:14.307 --> 00:01:15.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was even doing comedy
or any of that.

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:19.879
And it was interesting
doing this and directing myself,

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:22.182 line:92%
but, also, the other actors.

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:24.484 size:78% position:39%
They wouldn't know --
like, Sarah Goldberg,

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:26.152
who was in that scene --
she's great in the show --

00:01:26.152 --> 00:01:29.522
but she said she wouldn't know
if I was reacting in character

00:01:29.522 --> 00:01:31.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
or if I was reacting
as the director.

00:01:31.124 --> 00:01:32.725 size:84% position:42%
-[ Chuckling ] Right.
-'Cause she would be --

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:35.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
so, we'd be doing a scene
and I'd be going...

00:01:35.462 --> 00:01:38.431 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:40.633 size:81% position:41% line:92%
[ Laughter continues ]

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:44.504 size:81% position:41% line:92%
[ Laughter continues ]

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:46.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she's like,
"Is that -- Is that --

00:01:46.139 --> 00:01:48.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's --
That's the character, right?

00:01:48.007 --> 00:01:48.541 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's not you?"

00:01:48.541 --> 00:01:51.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I'm like, "No, no, no.
No, no. That's the character."

00:01:51.044 --> 00:01:51.611 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Uh-huh.

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:52.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
And he hates your acting.

00:01:52.946 --> 00:01:53.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, no.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.516 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, she -- No, she --
she's phenomenal on the show.

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:59.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You --
You have a fantastic cast --

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:00.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
Stephen Root,
who's a great actor.

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:02.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
The acting teacher
is Henry Winkler.

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:04.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, Henry Winkler is in it.
Yes.

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:05.825 line:92%
-Who is one of those people --

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm sure
you'll attest this, as well --

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:09.429
he came on this show --
he's one of those guys --

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:11.197
nothing would be worse
than if he was a bad guy.

00:02:11.197 --> 00:02:13.967
-No, yeah, he's the nicest
human being on the planet.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:15.135 line:92%
-And you need it to be the case.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:17.270 size:84% position:42%
You need Henry Winkler
to be as nice as he is.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:23.243
-Yes. And then we cast him
as a very angry acting coach.

00:02:23.243 --> 00:02:24.177 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:25.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And there is a scene
in the pilot

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:27.780 size:75% position:38%
where he has to make
Sarah Goldberg cry.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.415 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he's yelling at her
and everything.

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:32.952
And I went over. I go, "Henry,
you got to really go at her.

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:34.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like,
don't worry about the words --

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:36.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
you just got to, you know,
try to make her cry."

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:37.524 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And he pulled me aside.

00:02:37.524 --> 00:02:41.694
He goes, "Bill,
I need to understand something.

00:02:41.694 --> 00:02:43.830 size:84% position:42% line:92%
This man I'm playing --

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:46.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
he's an [bleep]"
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:46.266 --> 00:02:48.234 line:92%
I said, "Yes, he's an [bleep]"

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:50.036 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He went, "Okay."

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:50.670 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:54.207
And then, he did this take,
and he went at her so hard.

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:56.242 size:75% position:38%
And you were just --
We're like, "Whoa!"

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:59.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
And she was going, "Oh, God."

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:00.213 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It's in the show.

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:02.282 size:88% position:44%
She's like, "Wait, whoa,
Henry, what's going on?"

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:04.684 size:81% position:41%
He was just, like...
[ Shouting gibberish ]

00:03:04.684 --> 00:03:05.385 line:92%
It was like, "Oh, Henry."

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:08.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, deep down,
he's, like, a -- a maniac.

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:09.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:10.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
Good to find out, and now --
-He's a monster. No.

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:13.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And what
I'm so excited about is --

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.827 line:92%
tonally, it's unlike anything,

00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:16.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
not only have I --
that I've seen from you,

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:19.832 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I feel like very --
it's really funny, very dark.

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:21.701
-Yeah.
-Has some great action elements.

00:03:21.701 --> 00:03:23.369 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-And -- And did that

00:03:23.369 --> 00:03:25.572
just kind of come in the process
of -- of sitting down?

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:27.774
Or when you were like,
"I'm gonna do a show for HBO --

00:03:27.774 --> 00:03:29.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want there to be a lot
of action, as well"?

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:32.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
It's like if the guy from --

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.047 line:92%
you know, if -- if "Unforgiven,"

00:03:34.047 --> 00:03:36.282 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, William Munny
in "Unforgiven"

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:37.784 line:92%
or the guy from "Taxi Driver"

00:03:37.784 --> 00:03:39.986 align:start size:94% position:6%
met the people from
"Waiting for Guffman."

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:42.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:03:42.322 --> 00:03:44.157 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they were like,
"How much money do you need?"

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:48.027
-Yeah, they're like, "Boy,
that's the idea of the century!"

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:49.295 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:49.862 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"We love it!"

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:52.632
-You just -- you did a premiere
at South by Southwest in Austin.

00:03:52.632 --> 00:03:54.167 size:81% position:41%
-[ Chuckling ] Yeah.
-I've heard you saying

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:55.868
it's fun to go to
different parts of the country,

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
because of the way
people say "Barry."

00:03:57.937 --> 00:03:59.505 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, yeah.
In Austin, it was like,

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:02.842 align:start size:94% position:6%
"So, man, you're with the show
'Barreh.'"

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:03.676 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Light laughter ]

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:04.744 line:92%
And I was like, "Excuse me?"

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:07.780 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they're like,
"Barreh! Barreh! Would you --"

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.583
Yeah, and then -- and here, I
come to New York, and it's like,

00:04:10.583 --> 00:04:11.584 align:start size:94% position:6%
[New York accent]
"So, Bill Hader

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:15.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the show 'Barry'!"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.288 --> 00:04:17.190 line:92%
"It's 'Barry,' everybody.

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:18.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
Here he comes --
Barry, everybody.

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:19.392 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Come in here."

00:04:19.392 --> 00:04:23.496
And I'm like, "Oh, my God."
-"Barry" different places.

